 "notes": [
  "The shift dD(u) is the least move south of the mapped north bank top (along the receding direction, u kept) that gives a clear walk of 3.0 m from every north-bank building and structure front (layout.json footprints and base lines), with walkable floors counted as walk (the dining terrace S2.bld.river_terrace_23250, the jetty S2.str.jetty_27260); every prop and figure standing on the strip stays on the flat, with 1.2 m to pass it on its river side where it stands less than 1.4 m from a front (the shop tables and sitters, the eatery's benches, the stall, the cart and mules, the bank talkers, the east sheds' furniture); and the five trackers keep 0.4 m of flat ground south of their feet over a 4 m haul west along 逆水行舟's heading (people.json boats.boat_towed_mast_23632 run_m). Then held to at most 0.55 m of dD per metre along the bank and smoothed, never above the need.",
  "By stretch: the shop row u 20700-21450 -2.0 to -2.6; the open shop and tiled wall 21450-21850 -2.6 to -2.9; the trackers' bank 21850-22250 -2.9 easing to -1.1 (their 4 m haul); the white wall and gateway 22250-22400 -1.5 to -2.4; the long house 22400-22980 -2.5 to -2.9 (its front stands on the mapped bank top); the terrace 22980-23500 -1.7 to -2.6; the eatery 23500-24050 -1.8 easing to -0.6; the unloading yard 24050-24400 -0.5 to -2.6; the scaffold house 24400-25200 -2.6 to -3.2; the open shop and 沿河雅座 25200-25640 -2.4 to -3.0; the warehouse 25640-26290 -2.8 to -3.3 (the most: its plinth's front is the mapped bank top); the white-wall house 26290-26600 -1.9 to -2.7; the wattle fence and the great willow 26600-27080 -2.3 to -3.2; the jetty 27080-27420 -3.1 to -1.7; the lower shed 27420-27900 -1.9 to -0.7; 0 from u 28160 (the east wharf is 6-9 m wide).",
  "The S3 seam: dD is exactly 0 on u 20500 and grows at 1 m per metre (the painted bank itself rises 48 degrees there), reaching -2.3 by u 20700. The walk past the slatted fence's west run is 1.5 m on the seam, 2.0 m at u 20580, 2.6 m at u 20640 and 3.0 m from u 20700. The north shore meets the bank top on the seam at (149.37, 24.68), S2's mapped bank-top point there (the mapped shore point (149.03, 25.54) clamped to it along the seam, the lead's rule; S3's north bank ends on the same point): the bank widens from 0 there to 1.0 m by u 20650 and is under 0.8 m across until u 20700. The lead plans the seam's water with S3's plan.",
  "The built north shore is the built bank top less the bank's width (1.0 m of D, widened to 1.1-2.1 m where the bank runs aslant so that it stays at least 0.8 m across: the trackers' diagonal u 21450-22400, the yard and halls u 24050-25700), or the mapped shore where that lies further south, the two blended over 0.8 m (no hooks). The mapped est shores north of their bank tops (u 20500-21720, 23300-26650) are not used. Where the painted bank is a broad wash slope (the trackers' bulge u 22250-22400; the east, u 26650-28970, 2-6 m wide) the shore stays as mapped and the moved bank top only narrows the slope (east of u 26700 to 2.0-3.5 m): the boats moored there don't move for the bank.",
  "The terrace (S2.bld.river_terrace_23250) goes with the bank (the area agent's call: its defining relation is its front on stilts over the slope with the diners over the water): the shift runs on smoothly under it (-1.7 to -2.6), and the terrace and everything on its floor (its five diners, three tables, the chair and the bundle) move as one group by the bank's mean displacement along its front, dX +1.19, dD -1.99 (river.json moves). Its front then stands 0.72-0.73 m down the built slope, 0.27-0.31 m above the water's edge (painted: the front floor on posts over the slope, the stilts' feet at the shore), and its back 2.7-2.8 m off the hall behind it (S2.bld.hall_behind_terrace_23380): ground behind and the floor are the walk.",
  "The landing steps (S2.str.landing_steps_22950) go with the bank by its shift at their u (dX +1.60, dD -2.72), so they run from the built bank top down into the water at the moved terrace's west foot (0.15 m clear of its south-west corner); the jetty stays (the eating shed's raised plank deck at the top of the bank, with the shed's tables on it): the built bank top passes 0.5-1.7 m south of its front, and the great willow's foot (S2.tree.willow_great_27068, D 12.88) stands at the built bank's edge.",
  "The south bank (S2.grd.south_bank_20500, mound_south_bank_21420, south_bank_flat_21850, south_bank_spit_22400) and the reaches' south shores are as mapped: every south shore lies on the water side of its bank top.",
  "The river's east end runs on to the S1 seam (the lead's call, Run 2): the mapped shore of S2.water.bian_river_e turns south under S1's massive willow from u 28450 (est, hidden under the willow's head) and met the silk's bottom edge at u 28967, 1.5-2.5 m short of the seam, where grain boat 2's stern is painted hidden; at 0.6 of its type it could not lie east of grain boat 1 as painted. So the shore runs on from (266.19, 7.51) at u 28357 to (274.98, 7.2) on the seam, and the bank top of S2.grd.north_bank_26000 from (271.18, 10.24) at u 28600 to (275.85, 8.5) on the seam (a slope 1.3 m wide). The strip stops on the seam (seams west and east); S1's ground beyond the seam is land, so S1's bank meets this water on the seam line (a seam note for the lead).",
  "The reaches share their north-shore ends exactly at u 21850, 23300 and 26000 (each bank's shore is its reach's north shore, point for point; the bank tops share their ends too). W2's strip closes straight from its south shore's end on the silk's bottom edge (189.36, -3.34) to its north shore's end at u 23300; M and E have no south shore (the silk's bottom edge cuts the water; mist below): their south sides and M's west side along that closing are the builder's; E's east side is the S1 seam line from its north shore's end (274.98, 7.2) to the silk's bottom edge.",
  "Checked (gen/sections/canal/boats/plan.py, write_plan.py): walk at least 3.0 m everywhere from u 20700 to u 28160 (fronts to the built bank top, or to a floor's front); the bank at least 0.8 m across from u 20700; built shores never north of their bank tops; the five trackers stay on the flat over 4.2 m; kit_boats.water_strip builds W (179 triangles) and W2 (196) from these lines."
 ]
